; SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later

; =============================================================================
; SpacesApp — the Spaces page: the summary first, then the calendar, sheets,
; documents and the assistant
; =============================================================================
; One EVG tree, built again on every change, as Sliqtly's editor and the EVGUI
; demos are: `page()` builds it, the host paints `displayListJson()`, asks
; `hitId(x y)` what is under the pointer and mirrors `a11yJson()` into the DOM.
;
; The data is a SpSpace (SpacesModel.rgr). The calendar is EVGUI's event
; calendar card (EcBoard), filled from the space's occurrences; a move or a
; new event made on the card is written back to the space (`syncBack`) and
; the card filled again, so the summary and the calendar never disagree.
;
; What the host does that the tree cannot: read a file or the clipboard for
; an import, and save a download. A press that needs one leaves `action` set
; ("import", "export:<sheet id>") for the host to take.
;
; With `server` on (the Warden page) the space lives on a server. The app
; keeps an outbox of calls (`outOp`, `outBody`); the host sends the first,
; one at a time, and hands the reply to `answer` (or the error to `failed`).
; What the calendar changes is queued as save_event calls; members, invites,
; new spaces and the demo data go the same way. Text fields are EVGUI
; InputCtls; the host's text-input bridge edits them through `focusedField`,
; `fieldStateJson` and `applyEdit`.
;
; Entries have types (SpacesTypes.rgr, the schema the server shares): the
; Add menu offers the types of the space's words, and one form edits any
; entry — its date and times, ward, who, place, notes, the type's own fields
; and its cost. An event opens in the form from the summary (a click), the
; calendar (a double-click, or Enter on the selected event) and the lists;
; Backspace or Delete on a selected event deletes it, with Undo in the
; status line (Ctrl+Z). Lists shows the record and deadline types, Budget
; what the costs come to month by month.
; =============================================================================

